# Durable agent-draft scratch — expensive in-progress pipeline artifacts that
# must survive between sessions (attribution-sibling drafts, OCR page files):
# a multi-hour producer run is the costliest artifact the sibling pipelines
# emit, and /tmp cleanup has destroyed drafts before. The boundary is
# regeneration cost, not uniformity — cheap regenerable scratch
# (extract-source.py plaintext, worker fragments) stays in /tmp. Owners of the
# output paths: the prepare-transcript-sibling / prepare-ocr-sibling SKILL.md
# files and the attribution-producer / ocr-page-producer contracts. Contents
# are working state, never committed; only this .gitignore is tracked, so the
# directory exists for new sessions. (Distinct from scripts/scratch/, the
# throwaway exploratory-query tier.)
#
# Lifecycle — durable, not immortal: an entry lives while it is referenced by
# path from meta/BACKLOG.md / meta/roadmap.md (parked cross-session work named
# by the open item that owns it) or modified within the grace window; the
# scratch-hygiene pre-commit gate (scripts/tests/scratch-hygiene.sh) blocks
# the commit on anything else. Closing a work item includes sweeping its
# scratch — deletion stays human (age-based auto-deletion is the /tmp failure
# this directory exists to prevent).
*
!.gitignore
